  toolchain as the reason, listing an absent runtime, an absent compiler, an absent build tool
  and an absent local dependency cache. That premise was tested and no part of it held: a
  JDK 17 runtime, a compiler, a build tool and a populated local dependency cache are all
  present here, and they were the instruments of the run described here. The established style
  in this evidence tree is to state the verified fact and note what the plan anticipated, never
  to repeat an unverified premise silently, because recording an anticipated reason in place of
  an observed one would place a falsehood in an evidence file, which is the one thing this
  archive exists to prevent. On the same principle this file does not claim that no run
  occurred, because one did.
  The obstacle recorded by the earlier reports in this folder no longer stands. Those reports
  were written while exactly half of this module's remediation had landed, so the module's main
  source did not compile and the test phase was never reached. Both halves are present in the
  tree this run used, and the module now compiles, which is what made a capture possible here
  where it was not possible then. That change of circumstance is disclosed rather than passed
  over, so the difference in provenance between this report and its neighbours is explained on
  its face.
  The local file based artifact repository is not implicated in anything and is not blamed
  here. The run was performed offline on purpose so that this could be established, and every
  dependency the module needs resolved from the local cache with no network access.
  No runtime was installed in order to obtain this capture, no capture was simulated, and no
  dependency change is made or proposed by this file, in keeping with the scope and tooling
  fence of the rule labelled R-1 here. Beyond the build tool already present, only the POSIX
  toolset and interpreters already present were used, the latter to confirm that this file is
  well formed and that its counts and names agree with the source rather than to produce any part
